SIMPLE#ONIONS
IDEA#DAR#DROD
NL#SHINGLE#NO
GENT#FVA#SEEN
L#E#LYING#D#C
EIRLY#L#ROUGE
#IVORY#DANCE#
WROTE#A#FEATS
I#U#SPLIT#T#H
DASH#SIT#DEMI
OC#ALABAMA#AM
WHEN#LIL#DRUM
SELDOM#YEARLY


A1. Innocent. ~ SIMPLE
A6. Strong vegetables. ~ ONIONS
A11. The very first thing a writer gets for a story. (The last thing is money.) ~ IDEA
A12. Patriotic organization of ladies whose ancestors made them eligible for it. (Initials.) ~ DAR
A14. A very small quantity of amber colored liquid. ~ DROD
A15. Abbreviation for the Latin phrase "non licet." (It isn't common but soon will be.) Means "It is not permitted." ~ NL
A16. Something flappers get on the top that they should get elsewhere. ~ SHINGLE
A17. This is the word that takes all the joy out of life. ~ NO
A18. The male member of a couple at the Stevedores' Ball. ~ GENT
A20. Friends of Volstead Association. (If there is any such thing!) (Initials.) ~ FVA
A21. What nobody likes to be when coming out of a hock shop. ~ SEEN
A23. A man's wife can always tell when he's doing this. ~ LYING
A25. If you call a lazy man this he will get up and fight. (That is if he's not too lazy.) ~ EIRLY
A28. We would tell you this but it makes our lips stick. ~ ROUGE
A31. Beneath many a beautiful boyish bob. ~ IVORY
A32. Modern girls don't wear seven veils when they do this nowadays. (One is plenty.) ~ DANCE
A33. What most of the boys at college did for money last year. ~ WROTE
A35. Difficult stunts (like dressing in an upper berth). ~ FEATS
A37. What the rural judge and the constable do with the ten bucks the speeder donates. ~ SPLIT
A40. Something heroines make for safety. ~ DASH
A43. You can't do this in a telephone booth. (Has nothing to do with getting the right number.) ~ SIT
A44. We used to get Christmas cheer in this plus johns. Now we get it in this plus tasses. ~ DEMI
A46. Abbreviation for something wet and salty. (Pretty deep stuff!) ~ OC
A47. All song writers have a "home and mammy waiting for 'em" here. ~ ALABAMA
A48. What a girl comes home from a dance in. ~ AM
A49. An adverb, meaning the time that. ~ WHEN
A51. What Lillian's sweetie calls her. ~ LIL
A52. Something hard to beat musically. ~ DRUM
A54. Answer to the question, "How's the world treating you lately?" ~ SELDOM
A55. We just put this in to remind you when to subscribe for JUDGE. ~ YEARLY

D1. What a married man realizes he isn't when he comes home at 3 A.M. and meets the wife. ~ SINGLE
D2. What actors are when they aren't acting. ~ IDLE
D3. A pronoun. ~ ME
D4. If you have a shady one, keep it dark. ~ PAST
D5. What books and plays were once supposed to do for us. ~ EDIFY
D6. Many a man has marched forth to battle to the strains of this musical instrument. ~ ORGAN
D7. The day in March on which Caesar collected his "rents." ~ IDES
D8. Just to prove that this is a real C. W. P.— here's a co-ordinating conjunction that marks an alternative! ~ OR
D9. With how many wives would man be happiest? ~ NONE
D10. You can't drive a nail with one of these no matter how hard you soak it. ~ SDONCE
D13. A noisy chorus. ~ ANVIL
D19. How a man with something on his hip feels on a slippery day. ~ NERVOUS
D22. A teacher can't do this to a boy if he plays hookey. ~ EDUCATE
D23. Harps. (Not Irish.) ~ LYRES
D24. Why dry agents have cars almost as good as bootleggers drive. ~ GRAFT
D26. A Scotchman doesn't mind stopping at a garage for this. ~ IIR
D27. Some people think they know this. ~ LOT
D29. You can't throw this with a pair of dice. ~ ONE
D30. One thing that it's difficult to do with money. ~ GET
D33. Women whose husbands never annoy them. ~ WIDOWS
D34. What a man coming home at 3 A.M. thinks about. ~ ALIBI
D36. To shake the light fantastic shoulder. ~ SHIMMY
D38. The usual hymn has a silent last letter. This hymn has a silent first letter. ~ PSALM
D39. A boot in the map. (You'd better get out the geography.) ~ ITALY
D41. The first thing that comes into your head the morning after the New Year's party. ~ ACHE
D42. Napoleon usually had one in his coat. ~ HAND
D44. A childish thing to say. ~ DADA
D45. To beat and bruise or mangle; handle roughly. (This has nothing to do with a laundry.) ~ MAUL
D50. In the middle of hell. ~ EL
D53. This may be the last thing you cross if you don't stop, look and listen. (Abr.) ~ RR


